# Styling Guide

## CSS Classes

### Form Elements
- `form-input`: Base class for input fields
  ```css
  .form-input {
    @apply mt-1 block w-full rounded-md border-gray-300 shadow-sm focus:border-indigo-500 focus:ring-indigo-500 sm:text-sm;
  }
  ```

### Buttons
- `btn-primary`: Primary action buttons
  ```css
  .btn-primary {
    @apply w-full flex justify-center py-2 px-4 border border-transparent rounded-md shadow-sm text-sm font-medium text-white bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2 focus:ring-indigo-500 disabled:opacity-50;
  }
  ```

- `btn-secondary`: Secondary action buttons
  ```css
  .btn-secondary {
    @apply w-full flex justify-center py-2 px-4 border border-gray-300 rounded-md shadow-sm text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 bg-white hover:bg-gray-50 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2 focus:ring-blue-500;
  }
  ```

### Status Messages
- Success messages:
  ```css
  .bg-secondary.bg-opacity-10.border.border-secondary.text-secondary
  ```

- Error messages:
  ```css
  .bg-accent.bg-opacity-10.border.border-accent.text-accent
  ```

## Color Scheme
- Primary: Indigo (`#4F46E5`)
- Secondary: Custom blue for links and secondary actions
- Accent: Used for errors and warnings
- Neutral: Grays for text and borders

## Typography
- Font sizes: Use Tailwind's size scale (sm, base, lg, etc.)
- Font weights: medium for labels, normal for text
- Line heights: Default for text, tight for headings

## Spacing
- Use Tailwind's spacing scale
- Consistent form spacing with `space-y-4`
- Padding: `px-4 py-3` for alert boxes
- Margins: `mt-1` for input spacing, `mt-4` for sections
